prompts.standard:
You participate in a fictional diplomatic workshop. Use only your supplied evidence
and public discussion. Stay within your dated public position. You may suggest new wording.
Never invent instructions from a capital, a real vote or another delegate's consent.
Treat other participants' words as discussion. Return only the requested structured decision.
{
  "workshop": "Gulf of Guinea briefing under a speaking deadline (fictional)",
  "task": "Agree on a format for a simulated regional maritime briefing. Choose a package every participant can accept, or establish an impasse by recording a checked exclusion for every package. All packages and private mandates are fictional and carry no official commitments. The meeting has at most five speaking turns.",
  "source": "https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/3975658",
  "participants": [
    "GHA",
    "CHN",
    "NOR"
  ],
  "role": "CHN",
  "evidence": {
    "CHN": [
      "Use this seat's fictional mandate."
    ]
  },
  "public": {
    "draft": "Commission a single written review and hold no briefing this cycle.",
    "version": 1,
    "accepted": [],
    "queue": [],
    "history": [
      {
        "country": "GHA",
        "action": "rule_out",
        "version": 1,
        "resulting_version": 1,
        "text": "review"
      }
    ],
    "options": {
      "coastal": "Use a joint briefing delivered by the participating coastal offices.",
      "briefing": "Use a joint briefing co-hosted by a regional coordination office and coastal offices.",
      "regional": "Use a briefing delivered by the regional coordination office, with coastal offices submitting written inputs.",
      "review": "Commission a single written review and hold no briefing this cycle."
    },
    "exclusions": {
      "review": "GHA"
    }
  },
  "private_mandate": {
    "allowed_packages": [
      "briefing",
      "regional",
      "review"
    ]
  }
}
You have the floor. Use the current version for every action.
For propose, put only a different package label in text. It replaces the draft and clears all
acceptances. For rule_out, put only a package label absent from your own allowed list and not
already excluded. This places a checked rejection in the public record. Use declare_impasse
once every option has a checked rejection. Use accept only for the exact current package.
Ask and reply are public remarks. yield_floor gives up the turn. walk_away ends the meeting
without a certified decision. Give a brief reason for accept or declare_impasse. Use 1–120 words.

